 /*
- * ps3recomp - cellFont HLE implementation
+ * ps3recomp - cellFont / cellFontFT HLE implementation
  *
- * Font system with optional stb_truetype.h backend for actual TTF rendering.
- * Without stb_truetype, returns valid (but empty) glyph data so games
- * don't crash.
+ * The firmware font library as a title links it: libfont (cellFont*) with the
+ * FreeType-backed font library from libfontFT
+ * (cellFontInitLibraryFreeTypeWithRevision). Everything the title hands us is
+ * a guest address, and every struct is read and written big-endian at its SDK
+ * offset (cellFont.h). Glyphs are rasterized with FreeType when the build has
+ * it (PS3RECOMP_HAS_FREETYPE), else with the bundled stb_truetype.
+ *
+ * Memory: the library objects the SDK says the library allocates (the
+ * CellFontLibrary, a renderer's glyph buffer) come from the title's own
+ * allocator, the MemoryIF callbacks in CellFontLibraryConfigFT, called as
+ * guest functions through ppu_guest_call. Font file data and rasterizer state
+ * stay on the host; the title cannot see them, the same way it cannot see
+ * libfont's internals.
+ *
+ * Ported from the MotorStorm Apocalypse port's toolkit patch. MotorStorm:
+ * Pacific Rift imports exactly the same seventeen entry points. They are all
+ * implemented here (cellFontOpenFontset and a few other siblings are extras):
+ *   cellFontInitializeWithRevision  cellFontEnd
+ *   cellFontInitLibraryFreeTypeWithRevision (cellFontFT)  cellFontEndLibrary
+ *   cellFontOpenFontFile  cellFontCloseFont
+ *   cellFontCreateRenderer  cellFontDestroyRenderer  cellFontBindRenderer
+ *   cellFontSetScalePixel  cellFontSetupRenderScalePoint
+ *   cellFontGetHorizontalLayout  cellFontGetCharGlyphMetrics  cellFontGetKerning
+ *   cellFontRenderSurfaceInit  cellFontRenderSurfaceSetScissor
+ *   cellFontRenderCharGlyphImage
+ * It draws each glyph through a surface whose buffer is NULL and copies the
+ * bitmap out of CellFontImageTransInfo, i.e. out of the renderer's buffer.
+ *
+ * Behavioural reference: RPCS3's rpcs3/Emu/Cell/Modules/cellFont.cpp (GPL);
+ * no code taken. Where it and the title disagree the title wins -- e.g. the
+ * render position is the glyph origin on the baseline, which is how the title
+ * centres each glyph in a 4x-size scratch surface.
  */
 
